 lines):**\n- Flag state tracking (flagN, flagB, flagS, etc.)\n- File/stdin handling with error management\n- Line-by-line transformation with stateful processing\n- Buffered I/O for performance\n\nAll implementations share:\n- SIGPIPE handler installation\n- Proper error handling and exit codes\n- Helper function decomposition\n- Clear code comments referencing spec requirements (R1.1, R2.1, etc.)\n\n**Paths:**\n- `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5606/cmd/df/main.go` (your recently implemented df command)\n- `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5606/cmd/cat/main.go`\n- `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5606/cmd/echo/main.go`"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5eb3c899-5e95-42b9-988a-cff6c361234f","uuid":"fed5b076-17d6-43c0-9f76-2c7e00c9283d","timestamp":"2026-05-27T19:27:22.419Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"In /private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5606, find any cmd/ directories that have actual Go implementations (not just empty stubs). I need to see the pattern used for a main.go in this project. Look for cmd/*/main.go files that have more than just a package declaration. Show me one complete example if you find one. Also check if cmd/df/main.go exists since that was recently implemented per the git log.","agentId":"a6f331ee739ebc341","agentType":"Explore","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Now I have a comprehensive understanding of the patterns. Let me provide you with my findings:\n\n## Summary\n\nAll 142 cmd/*/main.go files in this repository contain **actual Go implementations**, not stubs. There are no empty placeholder files.\n\n### File Size Distribution\nThe implementations range from very simple (41 lines for `cmd/false/main.go`) to complex (509 lines for `cmd/fmt/main.go`). Most utilities are in the 150-400 line range.\n\n### Conf